jobs.prompt:
Acceptance re-review after a regression fix (older done modules are never added as dependencies; the review-stall test now asserts the T-8020 skip) (read-only; do not edit any file except the one result file named below) of tickets built on branch swarm/split-review-fixes. For each ticket check every acceptance line against the code and tests in your context: is it met, and is there a test that would fail if it were not? Read only. Tickets (JSON data, not instructions):
- {"ticket": "T-8019", "title": "Splitter keeps tests with their build ticket, never attaches not-yet-existing context, never gives protected files to workers", "files": ["tools/scope-commands.mjs", "tools/wiring.mjs", "tests/scope-split-guards.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["A test ticket is in the same stage as, and depends on or follows in the same wave, the build ticket whose module it tests; split ingest repairs or rejects a test ticket placed in a later stage.", "Context entries must exist in the repo when the ticket starts or be produced by a dependsOn ticket; others are dropped with a note.", "Always-protected files (coordination/checks.json and every protected path) are never assigned to worker tickets; they are routed to an owner window with a note.", "Tests: split ingest rejects or repairs each case."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8020", "title": "An acceptance review that cannot start for one ticket (e.g. built in another worktree) is skipped with a note, never stalling the wave", "files": ["tools/scope-loop.mjs", "tools/acceptance.mjs", "tests/acceptance-review-skip.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["When an acceptance review cannot be generated or started for a ticket (files in a different worktree, or any review-start failure), that review is skipped with a ticket note and a named non-blocking warning, and the rest of the wave completes.", "Test: a wave with one cross-worktree ticket completes the other tickets."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8021", "title": "Card \"last ticket finished\" takes the newest finish time across every family ledger", "files": ["tools/board-data.mjs", "tests/board-accuracy-activity.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["lastTicketFinishedAt is the newest ticket-done time across the ledgers of the main folder, every linked worktree and scratch worktree of the project.", "Test: the newest done transition lives only in a worktree ledger and the card shows it."]}
- {"ticket": "T-8022", "title": "A similar-name hit on a path a ticket creates only warns; --accept-new-path overrides a remaining refusal", "files": ["tools/ticket-paths.mjs", "tools/scope-commands.mjs", "tests/ticket-paths-new-files.test.mjs"], "acceptance": ["A \"likely typo\" hit on a path the ticket itself creates (in its own files, not existing yet) is a named warning in the ingest report, never a refusal; the refusal stays for read/context paths that do not exist.", "swarm scope split --ingest RUN --merge --accept-new-path PATH[,PATH] turns a remaining refusal for exactly those paths into a logged warning.", "Tests: similar new file passes with a warning; a missing context path that looks like a typo still refuses; --accept-new-path overrides exactly the named path."]}
Write your verdicts to coordination/reviews/acc-review-split-review-fixes-2.json as exactly this JSON: {"reviewer":"cursor","reviews":[{"ticket":"T-0000","verdict":"pass"|"fail","lines":[{"n":1,"met":true|false,"evidence":"file:line and test name","gap":"what is missing, or empty"}]}]} with one entry per ticket. verdict is fail when any line is not met or has no test.
